{%- comment -%}
  Product card labels — the New pill and the bar.
  Spec: docs/design/PRODUCT-CARD-SYSTEM.md (variation B · Paper, Veronka 6 Oct 2026).

  The card itself is untouched: image, title left, price right beneath. This adds
  a pill at the top right of the image and a wide rounded bar inset from the
  bottom of it, clear of the title.

  One bar state at a time, decided in this order:

    buyable   any edition is launched AND in stock   -> the per-product wording
    sold_out  an edition has launched but none is in stock
    dated     no edition is on sale yet, but a date is CONFIRMED
    waiting   no edition is on sale yet and no date is confirmed

  "Never sold out before launch" falls out of that order: a product can only
  reach sold_out once something has actually launched.

  Dates come from snippets/launch-date.liquid and nowhere else, so a card and
  the page it opens can never disagree.

  Accepts: card_product (required)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0

  assign any_buyable = false
  assign any_launched = false
  assign soonest = ''
  assign cta_variant = null

  for v in card_product.variants
    capture v_when
      render 'launch-date', product: card_product, variant: v
    endcapture
    assign v_when = v_when | strip

    assign v_launched = true
    if v_when == 'soon'
      assign v_launched = false
    elsif v_when != blank
      assign v_when_n = v_when | plus: 0
      if v_when_n > today
        assign v_launched = false
      endif
    endif

    if v_launched
      assign any_launched = true
      if v.available
        assign any_buyable = true
        comment
          A product with two editions on one card follows the cheaper buyable
          one: the e-book while only that is on sale, the printed book once both
          are. The visitor has not chosen an edition yet, so the card offers the
          one they are most likely to mean.
        endcomment
        if cta_variant == null or v.price < cta_variant.price
          assign cta_variant = v
        endif
      endif
    else
      comment
        Collect the soonest CONFIRMED date. 'soon' is not a date and never wins.
      endcomment
      if v_when != blank and v_when != 'soon'
        if soonest == blank
          assign soonest = v_when
        else
          assign soonest_n = soonest | plus: 0
          assign v_when_n2 = v_when | plus: 0
          if v_when_n2 < soonest_n
            assign soonest = v_when
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign card_state = 'waiting'
  if any_buyable
    assign card_state = 'buyable'
  elsif any_launched
    assign card_state = 'sold_out'
  elsif soonest != blank
    assign card_state = 'dated'
  endif

  comment
    New: one month from publication, computed here so nobody has to remember to
    take it off. Sold out beats New — at most one pill, ever.
  endcomment
  assign month = 2592000
  assign new_until = card_product.published_at | date: '%s' | plus: month
  assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign is_new = false
  if new_until > now_s and card_state != 'sold_out'
    assign is_new = true
  endif

  comment
    The wording. Written per product in the locale files, never assembled from a
    template: "Buy the deck" is right for a tarot and wrong for stickers. A
    product with no line of its own falls back to a plain "Buy", which is correct
    but flat — so adding a product means adding its sentence.
  endcomment
  assign bar_label = ''
  case card_state
    when 'waiting'
      assign bar_label = 'walterin.card.coming_soon' | t
    when 'dated'
      assign date_key = 'walterin.launch.date_' | append: soonest
      assign date_name = date_key | t
      assign bar_label = 'walterin.launch.from' | t | replace: '[date]', date_name
    when 'sold_out'
      assign bar_label = 'walterin.card.sold_out' | t
    when 'buyable'
      assign cta_kind = 'physical'
      unless cta_variant.requires_shipping
        assign cta_kind = 'digital'
      endunless
      assign cta_key = 'walterin.card.cta.' | append: card_product.handle | append: '_' | append: cta_kind
      assign bar_label = cta_key | t
      if bar_label contains 'Translation missing'
        assign cta_key = 'walterin.card.cta.' | append: card_product.handle
        assign bar_label = cta_key | t
      endif
      if bar_label contains 'Translation missing'
        assign bar_label = 'walterin.card.cta.default' | t
      endif
  endcase

  assign hover_label = ''
  if card_state == 'sold_out'
    assign hover_label = 'walterin.card.notify' | t
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_new -%}
  <span class="wui-cl__pill">
    {{- 'walterin.card.new' | t -}}
    <span class="wui-sr"> {{ 'walterin.card.new_sr' | t }}</span>
  </span>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if bar_label != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    A real link, reachable by keyboard: the buyable bar is revealed by
    :focus-within as well as :hover, so tabbing to it shows it. It carries the
    product title in its accessible name, because "Buy the e-book" on its own
    tells a screen-reader user nothing about which book.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <a
    class="wui-cl__bar"
    href="{{ card_product.url }}"
    data-wui-card-state="{{ card_state }}"
    aria-label="{{ bar_label | escape }} — {{ card_product.title | escape }}"
  >
    <span class="wui-cl__label" aria-hidden="true">{{ bar_label | escape }}</span>
    {%- if hover_label != blank -%}
      <span class="wui-cl__label wui-cl__label--hover" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- hover_label | escape -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>
{%- endif -%}
